00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Enter a new dimension of Strange.

2
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness is a fantasy,
action, adventure film directed by Sam Raimi.

3
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Doctor Strange, with the help of mystical allies both old and new, traverses the mind-bending and
dangerous alternate realities of the Multiverse to confront a mysterious new adversary.

4
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:46,000
Doctor Stephen Strange, played by Benedict Cumberbatch.

5
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:26,000
America Chavez, played by Xochitl Gomez.

6
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Wanda Maximoff / The Scarlet Witch, played by Elizabeth Olsen.

7
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:46,000
Baron Mordo, played by Chiwetel Ejiofor.

8
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:26,000
Wong, played by Benedict Wong.

9
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Dr. Christine Palmer, played by Rachel McAdams.

10
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:46,000
Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness is a 2022 American superhero film
based on Marvel Comics featuring the character Doctor Strange.

11
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:26,000
Produced by Marvel Studios and distributed by Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures, it is the sequel
to Doctor Strange (2016) and the 28th film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU).

12
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
The film was directed by Sam Raimi, written by Michael Waldron, and stars Benedict Cumberbatch as Stephen Strange,
alongside Elizabeth Olsen, Chiwetel Ejiofor, Benedict Wong, Xochitl Gomez, Michael Stuhlbarg, and Rachel McAdams.

13
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
In the film, Strange must protect America Chavez (Gomez), a teenager capable
of traveling the multiverse, from the Scarlet Witch (Olsen).

14
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:26,000
Doctor Strange director and co-writer Scott Derrickson
had plans for a sequel by October 2016.

15
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
He signed to return as director in December 2018, when
Cumberbatch was confirmed to return.

16
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:46,000
The film's title was announced in July 2019 along with Olsen's involvement, while
Jade Halley Bartlett was hired to write the film that October.

17
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
Derrickson stepped down as director in January
2020, citing creative differences.

18
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
Waldron and Raimi joined the following month and started over, adding elements of the horror genre that Raimi had worked with
previously and making Wanda the villain of the film, continuing her story from the Disney+ miniseries WandaVision (2021).

19
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
Filming began in November 2020 in London but was put on hold
in January 2021 due to the COVID-19 pandemic.

20
01:33:20,000 --> 01:33:26,000
Production resumed by March 2021 and concluded in mid-April in Somerset.

21
01:38:00,000 --> 01:38:06,000
Shooting also occurred in Surrey and Los Angeles.

22
01:42:40,000 --> 01:42:46,000
With a production budget of $350.6 million, Doctor Strange in the
Multiverse of Madness is one of the most expensive films ever made.

23
01:47:20,000 --> 01:47:26,000
Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness premiered at the Dolby Theatre in Hollywood, Los Angeles, on May
2, 2022, and was released in the United States on May 6, as part of Phase Four of the MCU.

24
01:52:00,000 --> 01:52:06,000
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and grossed $955.8
million worldwide, making it the fourth-highest-grossing film of 2022.

